# ESPHome YAML in this repo

## File roles
| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `my-sprinkler.yaml` | Full device config: must include `esphome:`, `esp32:`, connectivity (`wifi`, `api`, `ota`, `logger`, etc.). |
| `secrets.yaml` | Local `!secret` values; gitignored. |
| `secrets.example.yaml` | Checked-in template; dummy values only. |
| `packages/*.yaml` (optional) | Included fragments only — typically **no** top-level `esphome:`; merged into the entry config via `packages:` ([Packages](https://esphome.io/components/packages/)). |

## Conventions
- Prefer **`!secret`** for SSID, Wi‑Fi password, `api_encryption_key`, and `ota_password`.
- Keep the minimal “connectivity + OTA” baseline stable before adding sensors, relays, or packages.
- When adding components, match the **board declared in `my-sprinkler.yaml`** until a migration issue explicitly changes it.

## Security-related YAML (see [Security Best Practices](https://esphome.io/guides/security_best_practices/))
- **`api.encryption.key`** and **OTA password**: always **`!secret`**; do not reuse the same values on other devices in other repos.
- **`wifi:`**: use **`min_auth_mode: WPA2`** (or **`WPA3`** if everything supports it); **`ap.password`** must be **`!secret wifi_ap_password`** (or equivalent), never hardcoded in tracked YAML and never empty.
- **`web_server:`**: only with **`auth:`**; otherwise omit and use Home Assistant.
- **`logger:`**: default to **`INFO`** for production configs in this repo; avoid verbose Wi‑Fi/API logging unless debugging a specific issue, then tighten again afterward.

## Lawn irrigation (`sprinkler`)
- Official reference: [Sprinkler Controller](https://esphome.io/components/sprinkler/).
- Define **`sprinkler:`** with an `id`, **`valves:`** list; each valve needs a **`valve_switch_id`** pointing at a real `switch` (usually `gpio` / `hbridge`). Optionally **`pump_switch_id`**, **`run_duration`** or **`run_duration_number`**, **`enable_switch`**, **`main_switch`** / **`auto_advance_switch`** (required when there is more than one valve).
- **Do not** drive zone hardware from HA using the raw GPIO switches for day-to-day runs: use the **sprinkler-exposed zone switches** (`valve_switch` names). Keep underlying relay switches **`internal: true`** or omit `name:` so only the controller exposes safe entities.
- Orchestration from automations: actions like **`sprinkler.start_full_cycle`**, **`sprinkler.start_single_valve`**, **`sprinkler.shutdown`**, queue helpers, etc., keyed by the controller `id`.

## Packages (`packages:` + `!include`)
- Official: [Packages](https://esphome.io/components/packages/) and [`!include`](https://esphome.io/guides/yaml#yaml-include).
- In the entry YAML: **`packages:`** as a **list** (`- !include common/wifi.yaml`) or a **mapping** of labels to includes; mapping keys are labels only.
- **Local includes:** shared `wifi` / `api` / `logger` blocks, or templated snippets with **`!include`** + **`vars:`** / package **`defaults:`** for repeated hardware.
- **Remote Git packages:** no **`!secret`** in remote files — expose **`substitutions`** and assign secrets from **`my-sprinkler.yaml`** / local includes only.
- **Advanced:** **`!extend`** / **`!remove`** to tweak or drop nodes from an included tree; Jinja in **`substitutions:`** for conditional includes (see upstream examples).

## IDE note
- `.vscode/settings.json` maps **`secrets.yaml`** and **`secrets.example.yaml`** to plain **YAML** so the ESPHome validator does not expect an `esphome:` section there. For other `.yaml` files (including `packages/` or the main config), use the language mode you prefer in the editor.
